# HPO worked-example run artifacts.
#
# Each `run.sh` invocation rewrites these as a side-effect (~85 files
# per full sweep), polluting `git status`. The example *definitions*
# (README.md, config.hpo, run.sh, reference_fingerprint.json) are
# tracked; the runtime outputs are not.
#
# To regenerate fingerprints, see HPO/examples/tools/generate_fingerprint.py
# and `bash HPO/examples/run_reference_suite.sh --full`.

# Per-run output artifacts
best_*.tadah
loss.tadah
outvar.tadah
params.tadah
stats.tadah
pot.tadah
hpo_run.log
log.lammps
run.stdout
run.stderr
hpo_*_times.csv
asa_out*

# Bootstrapped seeds for INIT WARM examples -- regenerated on first
# run by the example's run.sh, not checked in (would otherwise embed
# the original author's filesystem layout into best_pot.tadah headers).
seed_pot.tadah

# 17_no_training_db intermediates: `tadah train` output + the pinned
# HPO seed derived from it, both regenerated by the example's run.sh.
hpo_seed.tadah
train.stdout

# Sub-directories created during a run
newBestPotsDir/
restart_pots/
prestage_pots/
hpo_optim_resolved.hpo

# Diagnostic tables written next to the run (search space, calibrated step
# scales, ladder history, Corana per-dimension acceptance). run.sh removes
# them before each run; this keeps a run's leftovers out of `git status`.
hpo_*.tsv
